# Zone

Work only in zone `tunetalez.com` on the TuneTalez Cloudflare account.

# Never touch

- Old R2 bucket used by the previous CDN setup
- `cdn.tunetalez.com` (legacy hostname)
- Production Pages / apex / www while doing staging-only Phase 1 work, except listing for conflict checks

# New resources (Phase 1)

| Resource | Name / hostname |
| --- | --- |
| R2 staging | `tunetalez-media-staging` → `media-staging.tunetalez.com` |
| R2 prod | `tunetalez-media-prod` → `media.tunetalez.com` |
| Pages staging | `tunetalez-web-staging` → `staging.tunetalez.com` |
| Pages prod | `tunetalez-web` (attach apex/www later) |

# CORS

- Staging media: allow `https://staging.tunetalez.com`, `https://tunetalez.com`, `http://localhost:8081`.
- Prod media (`tunetalez-media-prod`): allow **only** `https://tunetalez.com` (no localhost, no staging origin).

# Process

1. List existing DNS and buckets first. Stop and ask if `media-staging`, `media`, or `staging` already exist in a conflicting way.
2. Prefer custom domains over `*.r2.dev`.
3. If wrangler cannot attach a Pages custom domain, use the Cloudflare API with `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` — do not stop for missing wrangler UX.
